  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 5. Results (cold run, 150-digit numerics, `ψ = (1, 1/3, -4/3)`)\n\n- **Twisted states and Q-functions.** All 6 untwisted highest-weight states continue into their twisted weight sectors. Raw `q_k` have degree `4-μ_k` and raw `q^j` have degree `μ_j` (Baxter residuals ~`10^{-131}`). The twisted `T` tend to the untwisted ones with `O(ε)` corrections.\n- **Twisted identity.** `M^{AB}·w^{AB} = 0` to ~`10^{-117}` for all 30 ordered cross pairs, for all 9 raw rows and the 3 regularised rows. So the six columns `F_1..F_6` with `w = (Δc_1, Δc_{21}, Δc_{20}, Δc_{22}-Δc_1, Δs_1, Δs_2)` are the complete twisted system. `|w_{4,5,6}|/|w_{1,2,3}| ≈ 0.95ε`.\n- **Column hierarchy.** A raw row `(i≠j)` scales across columns as `ε^{(a,\\,a,\\,a+1,\\,a-1,\\,a-2,\\,a-2)}`, where `a` depends on the pair. So columns 4–6 are the least suppressed. Diagonal raw rows `(i,i)` vanish identically in columns 1–4.\n- **The untwisted 3×3 is the upper-left minor.** With the regularised rows `\\mathcal T_a`, `det A/det N_{untw} - 1 = 0.093, 0.0093, 0.00093` (max over states) at `ε = 10^{-3,-4,-5}`.\n- **Block dominance.**\n$$\\det M_6^{AA} = \\det N^{AA}_{\\rm untw}\\cdot \\det D^{AA}\\cdot\\big(1+O(\\varepsilon)\\big).$$\n  - This holds for 76 of the 84 triples of raw twist rows, uniformly over all 6 states. The residual is `≤ 9.1·10^{-4}` at `ε = 10^{-5}` over all 76, and `≤ 2.3·10^{-4}` for the `i<j` and `i>j` triples.\n  - The 8 exceptions are the six triples sharing an index `i` or `j`, then `\\{(1,1),(1,2),(2,3)\\}`, and `\\{(1,1),(2,2),(3,3)\\}` (whose `det D = 0`).\n- **Power of the lower-right block.**\n  - Rows `i<j`, `\\{(1,2),(1,3),(2,3)\\}`, which vanish at zero twist: `det D ∝ ε^{2+\\sum_{i<j}(μ_i-μ_j)}`, i.e. `ε^{10, 8, 8, 6, 6, 2}` for `vac, 10, 10̄, 8, 8, 1`.\n  - Rows `i>j`: `ε^{2-\\sum_{i<j}(μ_i-μ_j)}`.\n  - The state dependence `∏(φ_i-φ_j)^{±(μ_i-μ_j)}` is the familiar raw-Q normalisation. The universal `ε^2` is the genuine suppression of the three `O(φ)` integrals of motion.\n\n**Not yet done.**\n- Leading coefficient of `det D` on several rays: is it `∏(φ_i-φ_j)^{m_{ij}}` times a state-dependent constant, like the gl(4) singlet?\n- Replacing the raw twist rows by suitably normalised ones, so that `det D` becomes state-independent and `det M_6/det M_6^{vac} → N̂`.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 6. Everything over `M = 1/(ν_1ν_2ν_3)`\n\n`M(u) = ∏_α 1/[(u-θ_α)(u-θ_α-h)(u-θ_α-2h)]` has 6 simple poles. The ΔT_1 term already sits on it: `E_2 ν_1^{[-2]} = μ/ν_1 = M`. For ΔT_2 (degree 3 with twist) split\n\n$$\\Delta T_2 = \\nu_1^{[-2]}\\,\\delta_1 + \\nu_3\\,\\delta_2,\\qquad \\delta_1 = a_1u+b_1,\\ \\ \\delta_2 = a_2u+b_2,$$\n\nunique since `ν_3` and `ν_1^{[-2]}` share no root. Then `E_2ν_1^{[-2]} = M`, and `E_2ν_3` has poles `θ_α+{1,2,3}h`, which the full-contour shift `u → u+h` brings onto `M`. The identity becomes\n\n$$0 = \\Big\\langle -\\Delta T_1\\, Q^j_A Q^B_i + \\delta_1\\, Q^j_A Q_i^{B[-2]} + \\delta_2^{[2]}\\, Q^{j[2]}_A Q^B_i \\Big\\rangle_M = \\sum_c w'_c\\,\\langle G_c\\rangle_M,$$\n\nwith `w' = (Δs_1, Δc_1, a_1, b_1, a_2, b_2)` and\n\n`G_1 = -u Q^jQ_i`, `G_2 = -Q^jQ_i`, `G_3 = u Q^jQ_i^{[-2]}`, `G_4 = Q^jQ_i^{[-2]}`, `G_5 = (u+h) Q^{j[2]}Q_i`, `G_6 = Q^{j[2]}Q_i`.\n\n**Zero twist.** `a_1+a_2 = 0` and `b_1+b_2-6h\\,a_1 = Δc_1` (the `u^3`, `u^2` coefficients), so `w' = Δc_1(0,1,0,0,0,1) + a_1(0,0,1,0,-1,6) + b_1(0,0,0,1,0,-1)`, i.e. untwisted columns `H = (G_2+G_6,\\ G_3-G_5+6G_6,\\ G_4-G_6)`. The three `O(φ)` directions are `Δs_1`, `a_1+a_2`, `b_1+b_2-6a_1-Δc_1`.\n\nSince `w ↦ w'` is a fixed invertible linear map (it does not depend on the states), each new row is the old row times a constant matrix. The determinants only change by a state-independent constant; the cell checks this, and checks the rewriting term by term for arbitrary (non-difference) `ΔT_1, ΔT_2`.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 6. Rows over M = 1/(nu1 nu2 nu3): split of DeltaT2, identity, relation to the E2 rows, untwisted 3x3. ---- *)\nClearAll[polesM, pwM, rowIntM, colFunsM, splitT2, wM, rowTM, rowUM, colsH, arbCheck, detRatio, NhatM];\npolesM = Flatten[Table[{1/3, -8/57}[[s]] + n, {s, 2}, {n, 0, 2}]];\npwM = Table[1/Times @@ (p - DeleteCases[polesM, p]), {p, polesM}];\nrowIntM[F_] := pwM . (F /@ polesM);\n(* G_1..G_6 for dual Qa and direct Qb; the last two carry the u -> u+1 shift of the nu3 delta2 term *)\ncolFunsM[Qa_, Qb_] := {Function[x, -x Qa[x] Qb[x]], Function[x, -Qa[x] Qb[x]], Function[x, x Qa[x] Qb[x - 1]], Function[x, Qa[x] Qb[x - 1]], Function[x, (x + 1) Qa[x + 1] Qb[x]], Function[x, Qa[x + 1] Qb[x]]};\n(* DeltaT2 = nu1[u-1] (a1 u + b1) + nu3[u] (a2 u + b2): 4x4 linear solve on the u^0..u^3 coefficients *)\nsplitT2[dT2_] := Module[{x}, LinearSolve[Transpose[Table[Coefficient[Expand[b], x, k], {b, {x ν1[x - 1], ν1[x - 1], x ν3[x], ν3[x]}}, {k, 0, 3}]], Table[Coefficient[Expand[dT2 /. u -> x], x, k], {k, 0, 3}]]];\nwM[A_, B_] := With[{d1 = Expand[A[\"T1\"] - B[\"T1\"]], d2 = Expand[A[\"T2\"] - B[\"T2\"]]}, Join[{Coefficient[d1, u, 1], Coefficient[d1, u, 0]}, splitT2[d2]]];\nrowTM[A_, B_, {i_, j_}, mode_] := With[{f = If[mode === \"reg\", regFun, rawFun]}, rowIntM /@ colFunsM[f[A, \"dual\", j], f[B, \"direct\", i]]];\nrowUM[A_, B_, {i_, j_}] := rowIntM /@ colFunsM[Function[x, qpoly[A[\"qd\"][[j]], x]], Function[x, qpoly[B[\"q\"][[i]], x]]];\ncolsH[g_] := {g[[2]] + g[[6]], g[[3]] - g[[5]] + 6 g[[6]], g[[4]] - g[[6]]};\n(* term-by-term rewriting for ARBITRARY DeltaT1 (deg 1), DeltaT2 (deg 3), any (i,j), same state: E2 form vs M form *)\narbCheck[S_, {i_, j_}] := Module[{dT1 = 3/7 u - 5/11, dT2 = 2/13 u^3 + 1/3 u^2 - 7/5 u + 4/9, Qa = rawFun[S, \"dual\", j], Qb = rawFun[S, \"direct\", i], old, new, ab},\n   ab = splitT2[dT2];\n   old = rowInt[Function[x, Qa[x] (-(dT1 /. u -> x) ν1[x - 1] Qb[x] + (dT2 /. u -> x) Qb[x - 1])]];\n   new = (rowIntM /@ colFunsM[Qa, Qb]) . Join[{Coefficient[dT1, u, 1], Coefficient[dT1, u, 0]}, ab];\n   Abs[old - new]/Abs[old]];\ndetRatio[eps_, n_, tr_] := With[{S = tw[eps][[n]]}, Det[Join[rowTM[S, S, #, \"reg\"] & /@ TaRows, rowTM[S, S, #, \"raw\"] & /@ tr]]/Det[Join[rowsAt[eps][{n, \"reg\", #}] & /@ TaRows, rowsAt[eps][{n, \"raw\", #}] & /@ tr]]];\nNhatM = Table[Det[colsH[rowUM[s, s, #]] & /@ TaRows], {s, untw}]/Det[colsH[rowUM[untw[[1]], untw[[1]], #]] & /@ TaRows];\nWith[{S = tw[10^-3], S4 = tw[10^-4], trs = {{{1, 2}, {1, 3}, {2, 3}}, {{2, 1}, {3, 1}, {3, 2}}}},\n Grid[{\n   {\"rewriting E2 -> M, arbitrary ΔT, all 9 raw (i,j), all 6 states, eps=1e-3: max rel. diff\", N[Max[Table[arbCheck[s, ij], {s, S}, {ij, Tuples[Range[3], 2]}]], 5]},\n   {\"identity <G>.w' = 0, all A≠B, 9 raw + 3 reg rows: max |row.w'|/Σ|row_c w'_c|\", N[Max[Flatten@Table[If[a == b, Nothing, Join[Table[relRes[rowTM[S[[a]], S[[b]], ij, \"raw\"], wM[S[[a]], S[[b]]]], {ij, Tuples[Range[3], 2]}], Table[relRes[rowTM[S[[a]], S[[b]], ij, \"reg\"], wM[S[[a]], S[[b]]]], {ij, TaRows}]]], {a, 6}, {b, 6}]], 5]},\n   {\"O(φ) directions (Δs1, a1+a2, b1+b2-6a1-Δc1) / max|w'|, eps = 1e-3, 1e-4\", N[Table[Max[Flatten@Table[If[a == b, Nothing, With[{w = wM[SS[[a]], SS[[b]]]}, Max[Abs[{w[[1]], w[[3]] + w[[5]], w[[4]] + w[[6]] - 6 w[[3]] - w[[2]]}]]/Max[Abs[w]]]], {a, 6}, {b, 6}]], {SS, {S, S4}}], 5]},\n   {\"det M6[M-rows] / det M6[E2-rows], rows T_a + raw i<j, per state, eps=1e-4\", N[Table[detRatio[10^-4, n, trs[[1]]], {n, 6}], 8]},\n   {\"same, raw i>j\", N[Table[detRatio[10^-4, n, trs[[2]]], {n, 6}], 8]},\n   {\"untwisted N̂ from H-columns over M\", NhatM},\n   {\"equals N̂ of the E2 form\", NhatM === NhatU}\n   }, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
